  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Arrange the following compounds in increasing order of rate of aromatic electrophilic substitution reaction.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0057_14f22dabb6a9.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 137px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "d, b, c, a",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "d, b, a, c",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "b, c, a, d",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "c, a, b, d",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The more nucleophilic group will make ring more prone to aromatic substitution reaction. Benzene becomes more reactive towards Electrophilic Aromatic Substitution when any substituent raises its electron density.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0057_50964172b7ef.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 141px;\" /></p><p>In structure (a)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;group shows&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>&nbsp;effect. while in (b)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>OH</mi></math>&nbsp;group shows&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;effect. In (c)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;effect is shown by functional group and in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;both&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>OH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo></math>&nbsp;show&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;effect.&nbsp;</p><p>So Correct increasing order is :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math></p>"
  }
}